Hexagon HTP: the slot index from the host, the error report of a batch, and --chunks in the KL mode

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9, with patches 0001, 0002 and 0003 applied.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h           the slot index check, with a named reason
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-opnode.h              the unfused ops of a chain travel with the fused op
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp          index from the host, fallback to the unfused ops, error report
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-ops.h             the batch response names the first op that failed
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-ctx.h             the op context holds an error detail code
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/main.c                records the first failed op of a batch
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c        index from the kernel params, detail codes
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gated-delta-net-ops.c index from the kernel params, detail codes
    tools/perplexity/perplexity.cpp                 --chunks limits a KL run

How to apply, from the llama.cpp root:

    git apply patches/hexagon-fusion/0004-hexagon-htp-gdn-slot-index-from-host-and-error-report.patch
    cmake --build build-snapdragon -j

Push to the phone: libggml-htp-v79.so (ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/), libggml-hexagon.so (bin/),
test-backend-ops (bin/) and libllama-perplexity-impl.so (bin/, the llama-perplexity launcher
loads it). The batch response struct changed, thus the two ggml libraries must come from the
same build.

Problem 1: INVAL-PARAMS in the warmup decode with GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION_STATE=1

The warmup decode of common_init_from_params is one token at the start of a sequence with one
slot. A host replay of each check of the fused ops on that graph passes: s_copy[0] is 0, the
state table has one row, and all 36 chains match. Each other INVAL-PARAMS source of the DSP is
a thread count check, and the host computes the same thread count with and without the fusion.
The one input that the DSP reads as a value, and not as a tensor, is s_copy. The unfused
GET_ROWS reads the same value and never validates it, thus a stale value there is invisible
without the fusion. The batch response of 0003 gives no op attribution, thus the failed op
stays unknown.

This patch removes the read of s_copy from the DSP. The host reads the index at enqueue time,
validates it against the state table, and passes it in kernel_params[0] with a valid flag in
kernel_params[1]. When the index is not a row of the state table, the host logs the reason
("the s_copy index is not a row of the state table") and runs the unfused ops of the chain,
which travel with the fused op. Thus the fused graph runs with a correct index, or the unfused
ops run for that token, and the run does not abort.

The batch response now carries err_op, err_opcode and err_detail. The DSP records the first op
that fails, and each check of the fused ops sets a detail code. The host prints them:
    ggml-hex: HTP0 dspcall : dsp-rsp INVAL-PARAMS : op #17 of 96 is GDN_STATE_STEP (opcode 60), detail 0xa
If the abort remains, this line names the op and the check.

Problem 2: --chunks has no effect with --kl-divergence

kl_divergence reads n_chunk from the header of the base file, and the loop runs over all of
them. With --chunks N, the run now scores only the first N chunks of the file, and logs that.
